Ladybird enforces a meta element’s policy in its document’s own
policy container, so a policy in a document without a browsing context
never reaches the page that created the document. No engine lets it
reach that page: Blink’s ProcessHttpEquivContentSecurityPolicy()
returns early for a document with no window or frame, Gecko’s
CSP_ApplyMetaCSPToDoc() returns early for a document loaded as data,
and WebKit’s Document::processMetaHttpEquiv() hands the policy to the
document’s own contentSecurityPolicy().
